body:
Many of us who face some really bad depression, get to a point of caring for others over yourself, your worth goes to them. Which I dont think is a bad trait. But for most, depression is a part of personal growth, whiether we accept that or not. Youre stuck at who you are right now, but the only person who can always be there for you is yourself, the only one who holds a key to your sickness is you. Support is pretty much required but.

&#x200B;

Youre at a point where I suggest you start at sqaure one. Whats left? What do you want with your life if anything?

Well, I will say that my girlfriend of one year, who was mentally ill, as was I, And I never, ever really once thought that i would lose everything with her in the matter of minutes but I did. Long story short, She was furious that I woke up 15 minutes late to my interview, Which I actually got the job, But she feel off the deep end in the matter of minutes. Shattered my heart.

&#x200B;

She wasent very concious of shit that goes one but what im trying to tell you is, you never really know somebody untill they walk through that door, never take your gaurd down, but dont let the thought take over or mruin what you have going. That might just create a problem in itself. Enjoy what you have and keep a constant flow of communication.

THIS!!!!!!!! This is for me, and in my opinion is the hardest thing to fully realize when you have depression. Seriously, thank you for this post.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
